/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Full Analog Controls
//
// There are couple of options available. Make sure to uncomment one
// section for each or the patch will break!
//
// Option 1: Inverted Y
//
// This controls whether or not pressing down on the right joypad looks
// up or down. When inverted, it looks up similar to a flight control
// stick.
//
// When "normal" it looks down. Some people find this more natural.
//
// Option 2: Clamping
//
// This option is a work around for gamepads that use a circular stop
// vs ones with a square stop at the base.
//
// When the edge is circular, you cannot move the joypad 100% to a
// corner. Instead it only registers as 70% in one direction and 70% in
// the other. This means you cannot, for example, move forward and strafe
// at the same time at the top speed.
//
// When the edge is square, you do not have this limit to movement.
//
// Clamping makes it so the game considers pushing the stick 70% or more
// in any direction as full speed.
//
// TL;DR - Use clamping if your joypad has a circular stop at the base.
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Uncomment only one of the following two sections for Y axis
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
[Inverted Y]
